      "combat_tutorial": {
        "iniciativa": "That track up top shows whose turn it is: everyone runs to the center and acts on arrival. More Pace gets there first and acts more — up to 3 actions to the slowest one's 1.",
        "escolher_alvo": "More than one enemy? Tap whoever you want to attack to pick them as your target — kill the weakest first or focus the strongest, your call.",
        "bolinha": "That little ball is your menu (drag it to any corner). ATTACK costs nothing; TALENT spends PM and shows what it does — a Hexer's can leave a status on the target; ITEM uses a potion or a status cure."
      },
      "alvo_tutorial": {
        "farol": "Check the dot colors: red is required to open the way, yellow is optional (pays cash or items) and green is done — if it was a repeatable fight, you can come back and farm it. Walk up and the action opens by itself."
      },
      "ko_tutorial": {
        "aliado": "An ally went down? They're out for the rest of the fight, but the rest of your crew keeps swinging. Keep an eye on everyone's PV."
      },
      "xp_tutorial": {
        "regra": "Fight points aren't split evenly: whoever finishes off the most takes the biggest share. Beating someone way weaker than your strongest pays little (never under 5); taking on someone stronger pays double or triple."
      },
      "descanso_tutorial": {
        "recuperar": "Here the crew rests: 10 heals whoever's standing, 30 gets the downed back up too, and 50 is the full job — health, downed and status. Status only goes away here or with a cure."
      },
      "agiota_tutorial": {
        "emprestimo": "Short on cash? The loan shark lends — but you pay back 10x as debt, and every credit heal after that DOUBLES what you owe. Hit the ceiling and he heals you free, then throws you straight into the Fight Club to settle up."
      },
      "clube_tutorial": {
        "como_funciona": "The Fight Club is a betting pit: 3 rounds back to back, no rest. Win and you clear the debt AND take the neighborhood's cash; lose and they patch you up — it doesn't count as a real loss. But the buy-in comes on credit.",
        "cura_dobra": "Between rounds you can patch yourself up — but healing again DOUBLES what you owe. Running mid-fight keeps the debt as it was."
      },
